<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42941" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Schoeneus</span></b> , ei, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σχοινεύς,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a king of
				Bœotia</i>, <i>father of Atalanta</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 244</span></i>; <i><span class="en">246</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Schoenēïs</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>the daughter of Schœneus</i>, <i>Atalanta</i>, Ov. H. (15) 16, 263; <i><span class="en">id. Am.
				1, 7, 13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Schoe-nēïus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>pertaining to Schœneus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgo,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Atalanta</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 660</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Tr. 2, 399</span></i>; and <i>absol.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Schoe-nēïa</span></b> , ae,
				f., <i>Atalanta</i>, <i><span class="en">id. M. 10,
				609</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Schoenis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>Atalanta</i>, <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 14,
		14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
